cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FOCAL in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "FOCAL"
abstract: >-
  Foundation-model Contrastive Attribution: the genes that define a
  target-vs-reference cell state, found by running Integrated Gradients on a
  foundation model's embedding of a denoised pseudobulk centroid, contrasted
  against a chosen reference, keeping only the positive attribution channel.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
authors:
  - name: "The FOCAL authors"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/martinghl/focal"
url: "https://github.com/martinghl/focal"
keywords:
  - single-cell
  - scRNA-seq
  - attribution
  - integrated-gradients
  - foundation-model
  - contrastive
  - cell-state
  - marker-genes
  - bioinformatics
